  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 223 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nThrough next Thursday...\n\nDangerous heat will remain the primary focus through the period.\nThe strong subtropical ridge (597-598DM) will persist across the \nregion through the weekend into early next week. This will lead to\nincreasingly warm thermal profiles and strong subsidence across\nthe Gulf Coast region. Rain chances will remain squashed and\nshunted to the east-southeast through the weekend, with only\nlimited coverage. The humidity may drop a touch into Friday, but\noverall messaging of dangerous heat remains the same. No changes\nhave been made to the inherited heat HWO graphic and subsequent\nheat advisory through the weekend. Stay cool and hydrated and \ncheck on vulnerable populations.\n\nSome of the hottest days of the summer are expected, with highs\npeaking into the low 100s especially Sunday through Tuesday. \nThermal profile climatology (22C to 25C at 850mb) indicate \npotential analogs into the low 100s (101F to 103F and median\naround 102F), with some higher values exceeding that. Regardless,\ndangerously hot conditions will continue, even if we mix a little\nmore efficiently at times. Some portion of the area may need to be\nupgraded to a \"Significant\" risk and subsequent Extreme Heat\nWarning, but this focus looks far enough out in time to hold off\njust yet. The ongoing heat headlines continue through the\novernight periods with limited relief at night.\n\nRain and storm chances remain limited through the period, with\nonly peripheral areas seeing scarce showers and storm coverage, \nmainly into early next week. Some relaxation of the stout ridge \nwill occur into early next week. In conjunction with increased \ndeeper moisture, increased convergence from frontal zone sagging \nsouthward may cause some better rain coverage into early to mid\nnext week. Otherwise, dry conditions will persist most areas\nthrough the weekend. /DC/",
